turning the page, i'd like the "The Aeye" better if it created
portals to any level in any dungeon whether or not you've explored
there before and also if it had enough magic to override the
no-teleport effects of the "The Amulet".  one of the choices
should be "surface" which would allow you to escape the dungeon
(with all the caveats still attached).  something like:

#invoke the Aeye:
(you're a wizard in good standing, etc.)

Choose a destination (type ? for help):
A)  1 thru 28    Dungeons of Doom
B)  2 thru 11    Gnomish Mines
C)  1 thru 5     Quest
D)  1            Fort Ludios
E) 29 thru 54    Gehonnom
F)  1 thru 3     Vlad's Tower
G)  1 thru 3     Wizard's Dominion
X)               Surface

A24 (or "a 24" etc.)
(you arrive back on Medusa's Island Paradise ...)

this showcases the new multi-branch dungeon and makes the game a
little more comprehensible/accessible to those without source or
spoilers and makes the character class, in this case wizards,
_more_ unique.  IMO, arguments to the effect that this gives away
too much are bunk (he wrote politely).

the other quest artifacts could be, if needed (the PYEC is nearly
perfect for tourists alone as is), beefed up in terms of uniqueness
and game insight.

